<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Keflavík</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Keflavík is a town on the Reykjanes peninsula in south-western Iceland, now part of the municipality of Reykjanesbær. Its airport, Iceland's main international gateway, began as a US military airfield in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a>. Under a defence agreement of 1951 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> ran a naval air station there for Iceland, a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nato">NATO</a> member without an army, until the base closed in 2006.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/keflavik.jpg" alt="Keflavík" width="320" height="186" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: APK · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Keflav%C3%ADk_viewed_from_airplane.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
